rem Integer Partition Equations
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=207
rem Find the least m for which under
rem 1 in Q partitions 4^t = 2^t + k with
rem k <= m have an integer t

use bits
use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Q integer = 12345

rem With x = 2^t the equation is
rem k = x (x - 1), so each integer x > 1
rem gives a partition and it is perfect
rem when x is a power of two. To X the
rem count is X - 1 and the perfect ones
rem are the powers of two up to X.
Xs = 2 to (Q * 50) array
Pow = (Xs (Xs - 1) band) equal 0
Perf = (Pow choose 1 0) scan +
Low = (Xs - 1) greater Q * Perf
Hits = Xs filter Low array
X = Hits min
Answer = X * (X - 1)
Answer print
